g B4 for the B2-B3-B4 Chow is important. Similarly, keeping T4 for T3-T4-T5. So discarding F4 might be the safest option here. \n\nTherefore, the best action is to play F4. It's an honor tile, less likely to be needed for a critical meld by others, and it helps in not giving away a tile that's part of a sequence or pair in my own hand.\n", "output": "Evaluation: Playing F4 is the safest option as it's an honor tile not part of any critical sequences and minimizes risk of aiding opponents.  \nReason: F4 is an isolated honor tile with only one remaining in the unshown count, reducing the chance of others completing melds. Discarding it preserves key suited tiles (B2-B4, T3-T5) for potential chows and avoids exposing tiles in active sequences like W5/W6.  \nAnswer: Play F4"}
